A||||21||BroCar 87||Coupe and SPORT Coupe ? ? ?||||1||
Z||000000||BroCar 87||05-27-2000||01:09 AM||||Okey Dokey, What is the difference between the Coupe and the Sport Coupe? I was going to put Sport on my 87 coupe until i saw that there was a production style SPORT COUPE. I don't wanna immitate ( as the RICERS do with TYPE R) something that I don't have.<BR>TIA<BR>BroCar 87||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||05-27-2000||08:42 AM||||differences in 1987 were:<BR>coupe:<BR>14: steel wheels with covers std, no options<BR>22,603 built<P><BR>sport coupe:<BR>14" high tech optional<BR>wider tires also optional with the high tech wheels<BR>3,135 built<P><BR>interiors are both identical<BR>the 5th digit in the VIN identifies the car as a coupe("E") or sport coupe("M").||||reg||1
Z||000002||Motorhead||05-27-2000||08:51 AM||||Fiero 56. do you have the '86 differences and production numbers handy?<BR>Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000003||BroCar 87||05-27-2000||12:00 PM||||ahhh   here is a little on that... just the differences. not the numbers.  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.com/info" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.com/info</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||05-27-2000||12:32 PM||||1986:<P>econo-coupe: 9,143 built<BR>14" steel wheels with covers<BR>tires: 185/75/14<BR>seats: single color<BR>dash: single dark color, small emblem on folder type pocket<BR>instruments: color keyed bezels, oil pressure guage at bottom of tach<BR>a/c and auto are not available on econo model<P>sport coupe: 24,866 built<BR>14" hi-tech wheels optional<BR>interior same as econo<P>SE 4-cyl: 4,031 built<BR>SE v-6: 28,274 built<BR>GT: 17,660 built<P>All info is from my Fiero Spotters guide. There is much moore I left out on all models above. Too much to type.<BR>They are $5 each and are available from Mark Corbin at:<BR>Fiero Spotters Guide<BR>5474 S.R. 19<BR>Galion, OH 44833||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||05-27-2000||12:38 PM||||Looking at the link posted above, I can find many errors.<P>A few other than spelling errors are:<P>-SE available '84-'87, none were made in '88<BR>-SC available '84-'87, none were made in '88<BR>Also there were no SC with aero panels. All were in coupe body.<BR>-Formula was ONLY available in '88. And it was in the regular plain coupe body style. Nothing aero on it.<BR>GT was notchback in '85. Changed to fastback in '86<P><BR>Hope this clears up some confusion.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||05-27-2000||12:56 PM||||I checked the link and also the 84 and 85 SE's were coupe body styles 86 and 87 SE's were the AERO style.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||05-27-2000||01:20 PM||||Good point Orief. I missed that one. I am writing up a correct page right now. It will be on my site within an hour I would assume.<BR>The link to it will be:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/motorcity/pit/3490/modelinfo.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/motorcity/pit/3490/modelinfo.html</A> <P>front door to my site is: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/motorcity/pit/3490/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/motorcity/pit/3490/index.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||05-27-2000||04:27 PM||||The bare structure of the page is up. I will be putting more time into this page later. It will have to suffice for now.<P>Also, I am currently in the process of moving my page to a new home. Parts(soon all) of my site will be at <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero56" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero56</A> <P>The model info page is now at: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero56/html/modelinfo.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero56/html/modelinfo.html</A> ||||reg||1
