Z||000011||fiero56||05-28-2000||10:39 AM||||The fourth digit is supposed to be the body type. The Fiero being a P-body, the 4th should be "P". For some odd reason the 4th digit was an "A" in '84(according to spotters guide).<P>Just a little more fun info available in all spotters guides. This 80 page book has production numbers like in 1986:<BR>59.82%(50,230) of Fieros had sunroof<BR>42.03%(35,294) had had power windows<BR>in 1988 there were a total of:<BR>1,166 yellow Fieros.<BR>489 were coupes, 436 were Formulas, 241 were GTs.<BR>Also there were 730 '88s exported to Canada. With a breakdown of each model.<BR>TONS of info from these books. Everybody should get one.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Monkeyman||05-28-2000||11:28 AM||||Drew--Any idea what the difference was to the Canadian cars (other than maybe a metric change to the speedo)?  I can't seem to find my copy of the Spotter Guide right now.||||reg||1
Z||000013||overlord||05-28-2000||03:12 PM||||Fiero56,<P>my fiero is an 84 and the fourht digit is an "M"....there isnt even a p in the code at all.............unless my car is an 85??||||reg||1
Z||000014||overlord||05-28-2000||03:44 PM||||my bad...my fourth digit is A.<BR>fifth is M<BR>and there is a P in the middle||||reg||1
Z||000015||fiero56||05-28-2000||06:05 PM||||This is for all of us car nuts out there.<P><B>1</B>st digit = nation of origin<BR>1= USA<BR>2= Canada<BR><B>2</B>nd digit = manufacturer<BR>"G"= GM<BR><B>3</B>rd digit = make <BR>"2"=Pontiac<BR><B>4</B>th digit = series(body)<BR>"P" = Fiero<BR>"A" = Fiero in '84??? supposed to be for the 6000 series<BR><B>5</B>th digit = model<BR>"E"=coupe, econo, formula<BR>"M"=sport coupe<BR>"F"=SE and pace car<BR>"G"=GT<BR><B>6</B>th & <B>7</B>th digit = body type<BR>"37"=notchback<BR>"97"='86 GT fastback<BR>"11"='87-'88 GT fastback<P><B>8</B>th digit = engine code<BR>"R"=4-cyl<BR>"9"=v-6<BR><B>9</B>th digit = check digit<BR>various ones used<BR><B>10</B>th digit = year<BR>"E"=1984<BR>"F"=1985<BR>"G"=1986<BR>"H"=1987<BR>"J"=1988<BR><B>11</B>th digit = plant code<BR>"P"=Pontiac Motor<BR>last 6 digit are assembly order number starting with 200,001<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 05-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Ozzy||05-28-2000||09:01 PM||||Fiero56...<P>6th & 7th digits on the VIN for my '88 Coupe are 11. But it is a notchback, not a fastback as the decoding would state.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000017||fiero56||05-28-2000||09:54 PM||||Ok here it is corrected.<BR>"37"= '84-'86 notchback <BR>"97"= '86 aero fastback<BR>"11"= all Fieros '87-'88||||reg||1
